# .gitignore -- files Git must never track in this repository
#
# Infrastructure as code: the repository holds everything needed to rebuild the lab
# (Vagrantfile, provisioning scripts, the OPNsense configuration template, Ansible playbooks),
# but never secrets and never the local state of one particular PC. Both are created on the
# Windows host when the lab is set up.

# The lab's local secrets and SSH files (private keys!):
#   ssh/                                  the offline SSH CA (key encrypted, passphrase in DPAPI),
#                                         the PC's SSH key and certificate, the SSH trust files
#                                         and the lab's verified host keys (scripts/LabSsh.ps1)
#   ssh_config                            SSH client settings (scripts/Initialize-Lab.ps1)
#   pki/                                  the offline root CA: its key (encrypted), certificate,
#                                         revocation list, issued certificates (New-LabRootCA.ps1)
#   openbao/                              OpenBao's key shares and the PC's logins (DPAPI) and
#                                         its snapshots (Deploy-LabVault.ps1, Backup-LabVault.ps1);
#                                         openbao-retired-<date>/ after Remove-Lab.ps1 vault
#   opnsense/                             the firewall's passwords and API key (DPAPI)
#   ca/                                   the retired first lab CA (certificate only)
# Everything that the services use at run time lives in OpenBao, not here.
# Enterprise equivalent: secrets live in a secrets manager (HashiCorp Vault / OpenBao, Azure Key
# Vault), and its own first key in an HSM or a cloud KMS - never as plain files next to the code.
keys/
# A whole keys\ folder moved aside (for example before a rebuild from scratch).
keys-old-*/
# Note: vendor/mdad is a git subtree. MDAD's own vendor/mdad/.gitignore ignores roles/galaxy/
# (upstream installs the roles on demand); here they are tracked anyway, added with
# "git add -f" by scripts/Update-LabMdad.ps1. Tracked files stay tracked whatever .gitignore says.

# Vagrant's local state (machine IDs, Vagrant's own SSH keys for the VMs). Vagrant creates it
# next to the Vagrantfile; here vagrant\.vagrant is a junction to drive G:.
.vagrant/
